---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';

// Processing facts are carried forward from the existing policy, not inferred from other apps.
const CONTACT = 'arnavsharma8079@gmail.com';
const sections = [
  { id: 'local', label: 'Your local data' },
  { id: 'collect', label: 'Information we receive' },
  { id: 'google', label: 'Google sign-in' },
  { id: 'use', label: 'How we use information' },
  { id: 'storage', label: 'Storage and service providers' },
  { id: 'cookies', label: 'Cookies and analytics' },
  { id: 'retention', label: 'How long we keep data' },
  { id: 'choices', label: 'Your choices' },
  { id: 'children', label: 'Children' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact and updates' },
];
---

<Legal title="Privacy Policy - Intent"
  description="How Intent handles local task data, Google sign-in, device information and technical logs, plus storage, retention and your privacy choices."
  heading="Privacy Policy" effective="2026-10-09" sections={sections}>
  <div slot="intro">
    <p id="who" class="lead">Intent is operated by Arnav Sharma. This policy covers the Windows app and this website.</p>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="loop-card"><p class="card-title">Your work stays local</p><p class="card-body">Tasks, goals and reflections stay on your device.</p></div>
      <div class="loop-card"><p class="card-title">Account and service data</p><p class="card-body">We receive sign-in details, device information and basic technical logs.</p></div>
      <div class="loop-card"><p class="card-title">No advertising or analytics</p><p class="card-body">We do not sell your data or currently collect product analytics.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section id="local" aria-labelledby="local-h">
    <h2 id="local-h">Your local data</h2>
    <p>Your goals, tasks, focus sessions, interruptions, reflections, reviews, statistics and Kero settings are stored on your computer, not our servers. We cannot view, recover or delete this content for you. You control it by removing the app's local data.</p>
    <p>Intent does not record keystrokes, take screenshots, read your files or log the apps you use. Its fullscreen check only decides whether to hide Kero; it does not read window titles or app names, or store or transmit the result.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="collect" aria-labelledby="collect-h">
    <h2 id="collect-h">Information we receive</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google account:</strong> your account identifier, name, email address and email verification status.</li>
      <li><strong>Device:</strong> a random installation identifier, Windows computer name, Windows version and Intent version.</li>
      <li><strong>Account activity:</strong> internal account ID, creation date, last sign-in and service use, signed-in devices, sign-out times and session records. Session tokens are stored as one-way hashes.</li>
      <li><strong>API logs:</strong> IP address, request time, method, path, response status and duration. Logs exclude query strings, headers, and request and response bodies. IP addresses are also used briefly in memory to limit sign-in requests.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="google" aria-labelledby="google-h">
    <h2 id="google-h">Google sign-in</h2>
    <p>You sign in directly with Google in your browser. We never receive your Google password. Intent requests <code>openid</code>, <code>email</code> and <code>profile</code> permissions to identify your account across devices, not access to Gmail, Drive, Calendar or contacts.</p>
    <p>We do not request Google refresh tokens or store Google's sign-in tokens after authentication. Google information is not sold or used for advertising.</p>
    <p>You can revoke access in <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener">Google's third-party access settings</a>. See also <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="use" aria-labelledby="use-h">
    <h2 id="use-h">How we use information</h2>
    <p>We use account and technical information to manage sign-in and sign-out, recognise your devices, end invalid sessions, prevent misuse, investigate errors and maintain service reliability.</p>
    <p>We do not sell personal information, use it for advertising or share it with data brokers. We may disclose information when required by law.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="storage" aria-labelledby="storage-h">
    <h2 id="storage-h">Storage and service providers</h2>
    <p>Account data and private backups are stored in Google Cloud's Mumbai, India region (<code>asia-south1</code>). If you use Intent outside India, this information is transferred to and processed in India. Your local sign-in session is stored in Windows Credential Manager.</p>
    <ul id="services">
      <li><strong>Google:</strong> account authentication, server hosting and backups.</li>
      <li><strong>Hostinger:</strong> domain and DNS services for intentapp.app.</li>
      <li><strong>Let's Encrypt:</strong> API HTTPS certificates; it does not receive account information.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3 id="security">Security</h3>
    <p>App-to-API traffic uses HTTPS. Database access is limited to the API on the same server, administrative access is restricted, and direct internet SSH access is disabled. Sign-in uses one-time checks and hashed session tokens. Server secrets are not included in the app.</p>
    <p>No system guarantees absolute security. Local data also depends on the security of your Windows account and device.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="cookies" aria-labelledby="cookies-h">
    <h2 id="cookies-h">Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>This website does not set cookies or use tracking scripts. Fonts are served locally. The website server may process standard request information, including your IP address, to deliver pages. The app does not use advertising identifiers.</p>
    <p id="analytics">Intent currently sends no product analytics or usage telemetry and uses no third-party analytics or advertising networks. Before introducing analytics, we will update this policy, limit collection to specified usage events and obtain consent where required.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="retention" aria-labelledby="retention-h">
    <h2 id="retention-h">How long we keep data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account information:</strong> while your account exists; deletion is available by email.</li>
      <li><strong>Sessions:</strong> expire after 60 days without use. Expired records may remain until cleaned up.</li>
      <li><strong>Web access logs:</strong> 30 days, including IP addresses.</li>
      <li><strong>API logs:</strong> retained for a limited time and rotated at their size limit.</li>
      <li><strong>Backups:</strong> up to about four months. Deleted information may remain in older backups until they expire.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="choices" aria-labelledby="choices-h">
    <h2 id="choices-h">Your choices</h2>
    <p>You can sign out in the app, revoke Google's access permission, or remove local data from your computer.</p>
    <p>For access, correction or account deletion, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a> from your account email address. Account deletion is handled by email; an in-app deletion option is not yet available. Depending on your location, you may have additional rights under applicable law. Contact us to make a request.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="children" aria-labelledby="children-h">
    <h2 id="children-h">Children</h2>
    <p>Intent is intended for ages 13 and older, subject to additional local age or consent requirements. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. Contact us if a child under 13 has created an account so we can delete it.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-h">
    <h2 id="contact-h">Contact and updates</h2>
    <p>For privacy questions or requests, contact Arnav Sharma at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.</p>
    <p id="changes">We will update this policy and its effective date when our practices change. For significant changes, we will take reasonable steps to notify you through this website or the app before they take effect.</p>
  </section>
</Legal>
